  "statement": "Evaluate $\\\\int_{0}^{\\\\pi/2}\\\\sin^{2}x\\\\cos^{2}x\\\\,dx$.",
  "solution": "$\\\\sin^{2}x\\\\cos^{2}x=\\\\tfrac14\\\\sin^{2}2x=\\\\tfrac18(1-\\\\cos4x)$. Hence $\\\\int_{0}^{\\\\pi/2}\\\\tfrac18(1-\\\\cos4x)\\\\,dx=\\\\tfrac18\\\\bigl[x-\\\\tfrac14\\\\sin4x\\\\bigr]_{0}^{\\\\pi/2}=\\\\tfrac18\\\\cdot\\\\tfrac{\\\\pi}{2}=\\\\tfrac{\\\\pi}{16}$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Use $\\\\sin2x=2\\\\sin x\\\\cos x$.",
    "Then $\\\\sin^{2}2x=\\\\tfrac12(1-\\\\cos4x)$."
  ],
